        "root_concepts": "[reactor, physics]",
        "section": "nuclear",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "02 - Reactor Physics",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Nuclear reactor design is the engineering of a self-sustaining neutron chain reaction.\nThe challenge: balance neutron production against all loss mechanisms (absorption + leakage)\nto hold k_eff exactly at 1.000, then **control** it with small reactivity changes."
    },
